-XPR-3DGS is a point-based differentiable rendering method that implements 3D Gaussian Splatting within the XPR framework [S1, unofficial]. It projects 3D Gaussians to 2D, culls tiles based on conic bounds, and evaluates alpha blending per pixel [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by providing a high-level, Python-based implementation that requires significantly fewer lines of code than traditional C++/CUDA implementations, while maintaining comparable visual fidelity [S1, unofficial].
